WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.218
Vinnie and Mikhail rode down the streets of St. Petersburg.

2
00:00:05.219 --> 00:00:11.689
The buildings were grand but old, and birds had built nests in the stone cracks.

3
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.428
Vinnie saw that many people were poor.

4
00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:19.980
Children with sad, hungry eyes were in the streets.

5
00:00:19.981 --> 00:00:25.846
The old people sitting in front of the buildings looked tired and sick.

6
00:00:25.847 --> 00:00:31.230
"People don’t look very happy," Vinnie said to Mikhail.

7
00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.392
Mikhail nodded sadly.

8
00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:38.033
"Many people are angry at the royal family.

9
00:00:38.034 --> 00:00:42.182
The czar does not know how people really live."

10
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:47.628
"Mikhail," his father said, sharply. "Keep silent."

11
00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:54.200
"But, Papa, even you said that change must happen!" Mikhail cried.

12
00:00:54.201 --> 00:00:57.014
"We do not speak of these matters in the street,"

13
00:00:57.015 --> 00:01:00.235
Mikhail’s father said nervously.

14
00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:03.413
"The czar’s spies are everywhere."

15
00:01:03.414 --> 00:01:07.452
Inside the palace, Mandy was in trouble.

16
00:01:07.453 --> 00:01:11.914
The ruffle of Anna’s dress was muddy and stained.

17
00:01:11.915 --> 00:01:15.978
"Clean this up now!" said Anna.

18
00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:21.359
She pulled the ruffle off her dress and handed it to Mandy.

19
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.539
Then a servant led the ballerina down a hallway.

20
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.248
As she walked off, Anna’s dress looked shorter and very plain.

21
00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:35.474
Another servant motioned to Mandy:

22
00:01:35.475 --> 00:01:37.096
"Come to the kitchen!

23
00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.350
We’ll clean it there."

24
00:01:39.351 --> 00:01:44.170
In the halls and rooms of the palace, everything shone.

25
00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:48.076
It was as if gold had been poured on the walls.

26
00:01:48.077 --> 00:01:52.988
The furniture was covered in thick purple and red velvet.

27
00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:57.316
Crystal lights sparkled.

28
00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:01.910
"First time in the Winter Palace?" asked the servant.

29
00:02:01.911 --> 00:02:07.364
"Yes, it’s beautiful," Mandy exclaimed.

30
00:02:07.365 --> 00:02:11.005
"The royal family is usually here only in winter.

31
00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:16.819
But this year, the Romanovs are staying longer," explained the servant.

32
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:23.351
"Romanov . . . that name sounds familiar," Mandy

33
00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:29.899
thought. Outside the kitchen, they passed delivery men carrying baskets of

34
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.782
flowers. A little while earlier, Vinnie had arrived at the

35
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:41.125
palace. In the square outside, he unloaded baskets of flowers from a

36
00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:47.510
wagon. "Wow! Look at how big the palace is!" he cried,

37
00:02:47.511 --> 00:02:52.298
staring. "Come, we have work to do," said Mikhail’s

38
00:02:52.299 --> 00:02:59.177
father. Inside, Vinnie passed a servant and a little girl carrying some wrinkled

39
00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:06.132
fabric. The tall basket of flowers blocked his vision, and he didn’t see that it was

40
00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:10.458
Mandy. Mandy cleaned the ruffle as best as she

41
00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:15.210
could. Then she left the kitchen to take it to Miss

42
00:03:15.211 --> 00:03:20.087
Pavlova. She paused in a hall to look at a royal family

43
00:03:20.088 --> 00:03:26.485
portrait. In the painting, there were five children—four girls and a young

44
00:03:26.486 --> 00:03:33.872
boy."Romanov . . . ," Mandy said aloud, looking more closely at the picture.

45
00:03:33.873 --> 00:03:35.430
"Awful, isn’t it?"

46
00:03:35.431 --> 00:03:40.662
said a girl a bit older than Mandy who was standing nearby.

47
00:03:40.663 --> 00:03:45.599
She wore a pink dress with matching ribbons in her hair.

48
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:51.136
"I think it’s a fine picture," Mandy said nervously.

49
00:03:51.137 --> 00:03:53.590
"It doesn’t look like me at all,"

50
00:03:53.591 --> 00:03:56.503
the girl complained playfully.

51
00:03:56.504 --> 00:04:00.004
Mandy looked at the picture again.

52
00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:04.894
This girl must be the one sitting to the right of the boy.

53
00:04:04.895 --> 00:04:09.681
"You do look better in real life," admitted Mandy.

54
00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:13.422
The girl looked curiously at Mandy.

55
00:04:13.423 --> 00:04:16.222
Then she said, "I like you.

56
00:04:16.223 --> 00:04:18.679
You’re very honest."

57
00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.993
Mandy smiled. "I’m Mandy.

58
00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:24.438
I need to find Miss Pavlova.

59
00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:26.981
Do you know where she is?"

60
00:04:26.982 --> 00:04:31.155
"Yes. She is with my parents," replied the girl.

61
00:04:31.156 --> 00:04:38.266
"My name is Anastasia."

